// the themata (texts); the themata (reconstructions).
// Authoring brief: scratchpad PHIL801_AUTHORING_BRIEF.md. Syllabus:
// docs/academy/PHIL_801_SYLLABUS.md. Shape: Phil801Session (phil801.ts).
//
// Derivation conventions used in this file (Bobzien 1996, p. 153):
//   A1 to A5   the five indemonstrables, with their subtypes
//   T1         from A1, A2 ⊢ C infer A1, c(C) ⊢ c(A2), or A2, c(C) ⊢ c(A1);
//              c(X) is the contradictory of X, read as toggle: c(not p) = p
//   T1+        T1 for an argument with n premisses (Bobzien's extension)
//   T2         from A1, A2 ⊢ A3 and Ai, A3 ⊢ C (i = 1 or 2) infer A1, A2 ⊢ C
//   T3         from A1, A2 ⊢ A3 and A3, E1 .. En ⊢ C infer A1, A2, E1 .. En ⊢ C
//   T4         from A1, A2 ⊢ A3 and A3, Ai, E1 .. En ⊢ C infer A1, A2, E1 .. En ⊢ C
// Every derivation is written forward (synthesis) so that each line can be
// checked; the Stoic procedure runs the same lines backward (analysis).

